<article class="env-proposition" id="49A1CD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/49A1CD">Proposition <span data-tag="49A1CD">6.2.2.5</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small $\infty $-category containing an object $C$, and let $j: \calC \rightarrow \calP (\calC )$ be the Yoneda embedding. The construction described above yields a bijection </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  ( i: U \rightarrow j(C) ) \mapsto \calC _{/C}(U) \]
</div>
  <p> from $\Sub (j(C))$ to the set of all sieves on $C$. </p>
</article>
